>>* How to get rid of cursed items
>
>	There's lots of ways to rid yourself of a cursed item.  Get a
>nymph to steal it from you.  Eat a tin of deep-fried something-or-
>other (only works on weapons and rings).  Read a scroll of destroy
>armor over it (only works on armor, obviously).  The most common
>method for uncursing an item is to #dip it into a potion of holy
>water.  Be sure it's not *unholy* water.  (:

Don't forget that trusty old remove curse scroll.  You can also pray.
or polymorph into something that cannot wear the armor.  

>>* How to cure being a were-beast
>
>	There are three cures that I can think of.  Eat a clove of
>garlic or a sprig of wolfsbane.  Drink a potion of holy water (useful
>stuff, that).  #Pray.

>>* How to cure bad luck
>
>	Just wait it out.  Under normal circumstances your luck
>gradually drifts toward 0 over a few hundred turns.  The exception to
>this is if you're carrying a luckstone (normally appears as a single
>gray stone).  Uncursed luckstones keep your luck from zero-izing
>normally.  Blessed ones sustain only good luck and cursed ones sustain
>only bad.  There are many things you can do to raise your luck, but
>imho patience is the most effective.

Throw gems at co-aligned unicorns.  This is the fastest way.
Also, sacrificing certain corpses ( > geckos or cave spiders) will increase
luck a point at a time.
Patience is pretty good except in heaven...

